SCRIPTS=[
["China’s EV boom became a race for survival.","A 2018 report put the number of electric-vehicle manufacturers at nearly five hundred."],
["The capital commitments were enormous.","Reported funding ranged from around eight point four billion yuan at Byton to around thirty-five billion at WM Motor.","These figures describe funding, not cash losses."],
["Byton reportedly raised eight point four billion yuan without reaching mass production.","Saleen received six point six billion in state-backed investment, yet reportedly sold just thirty-one Maimai cars."],
["Around 2014, policy support and Tesla’s patent pledge helped fuel optimism.","Entrants from technology, property and consumer electronics saw an opportunity.","But entering the market was easier than mastering automotive manufacturing."],
["Venture capital backed ambitious growth stories.","Local governments offered land, facilities and industrial funding, seeking jobs, tax revenue and economic development.","But financing a factory was only the beginning."],
["For some startups, fundraising moved faster than manufacturing readiness.","Launch events promised the future, while production schedules slipped.","Suppliers, quality control and working capital remained critical."],
["From 2020, shutdowns and restructurings exposed the risks.","A review of fifteen troubled EV firms put disclosed funding above one hundred billion yuan."],
["WM Motor illustrates the balance-sheet risk.","Reported liabilities were about five times book assets.","Asset coverage was under twenty percent. Book values do not guarantee recovery."],
["By 2025, surviving brands had reached substantial scale.","The selected delivery figures show very different volumes.","But deliveries alone do not establish profitability, or guarantee a supplier’s long-term continuity."],
["Price competition puts margins under pressure.","The next test is sustaining the business behind each vehicle."],
["Three lessons: verify manufacturing capability, examine funding obligations, and assess margins alongside sales scale.","Supplier continuity matters."],
["Follow UNILAND MOTORS for Chinese vehicle sourcing and market insights."]]
